// activeSessionInteractionThreshold is the maximum age of LastInteractionTime
// for an ACTIVE session to be considered "genuinely active" (agent currently running).
// Sessions with interactions older than this are treated as stale (agent was killed)
// and must pass the overlap check to be condensed.
//
// This must be generous because LastInteractionTime is only updated on agent
// lifecycle events (TurnStart, TurnEnd, SessionStop), NOT on individual tool
// calls or git hooks. During a long turn, the only update is at TurnStart, so
// LastInteractionTime reflects when the turn began — not when the agent last
// did something. A complex multi-hour refactoring turn would have
// LastInteractionTime several hours old when the agent finally commits.
//
// 24 hours is safe: no single agent turn lasts a full day, but a killed agent
// from yesterday is clearly stale. The worst case is a stale session killed
// <24h ago gets one extra condensation — it preserves the data and on the next
// commit (>24h later) the overlap check prevents further zombie condensation.

